{"id":16,"date":"2025-05-04T06:18:05","date_gmt":"2025-05-04T06:18:05","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/?page_id=16"},"modified":"2026-04-21T02:43:34","modified_gmt":"2026-04-21T02:43:34","slug":"about-me","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/about-me\/","title":{"rendered":"About me"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull is-light has-contrast-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-917a35e9ac6531fad7c623a16a5da1e6\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-base-background-color has-background-dim-100 has-background-dim\"><\/span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-974f8fa9 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1067\" height=\"1067\" src=\"https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-42\" style=\"object-fit:cover;width:379px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited.jpeg 1067w, https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited-300x300.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited-150x150.jpeg 150w, https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/Sue-edited-768x768.jpeg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1067px) 100vw, 1067px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide are-vertically-aligned-top is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-ca2dd60b wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-top is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:100%\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-content-justification-stretch is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-d8dce8eb wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left\" style=\"font-size:clamp(0.984rem, 0.984rem + ((1vw - 0.2rem) * 0.938), 1.5rem);font-style:normal;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.4\">Surya Haridasan (she\/her)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">I grew up between cultural contexts, raised in Doha and rooted in Kerala, constantly observing how environment shapes identity, aspiration, and access. That curiosity eventually became design.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Before entering the world of product, I worked in retail operations, navigating policy, enforcement, and systems from the inside. That experience sharpened my understanding of how processes impact real people, a perspective I still carry into digital ecosystems today.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">My academic journey through sociology, political science, and economics continues to influence how I see design: not as surface-level problem solving, but as a way to question assumptions, redistribute clarity, and build more equitable structures.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">I\u2019m especially drawn to projects that sit at the intersection of culture, behavior, and technology, where the stakes are not just usability, but meaning.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Outside of work, I\u2019m usually in conversation about feminist art memes, cinema dialogues that feel like poetry, or the small idiosyncrasies that reveal how people really think. I believe context matters. I believe people are love. And I believe good design begins with paying attention.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Hi there!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I\u2019m a senior product designer who thrives on <strong>collaboration<\/strong> and <strong>independent problem-solving<\/strong>, equally comfortable leading a team or contributing as part of a group. The rush I get from <strong>solving complex problems<\/strong> is what drives me\u2014whether it\u2019s breaking down a user pain point or crafting a design that turns a challenge into an opportunity.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With a background in <strong>sociology<\/strong>, <strong>political science<\/strong>, and <strong>economics<\/strong>, I approach design with a deep understanding of <strong>human behavior<\/strong> and societal impact. I\u2019m passionate about <strong>research<\/strong>, but I\u2019m also highly focused on aligning <strong>business goals<\/strong> with <strong>user needs<\/strong>, ensuring that every design decision serves both the user and the brand.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To me, design isn\u2019t just about functionality; it\u2019s about creating a <strong>narrative<\/strong>, adding <strong>delight<\/strong> and <strong>aesthetics<\/strong> that turn a simple interface into a seamless, engaging experience. The combination of <strong>empathy<\/strong> and <strong>storytelling<\/strong> guides every project I undertake, allowing me to create solutions that resonate with users and create real impact.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-16","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/surya.free.gen.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/16","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}